[thin] Unavoidable without moving the stack's clamp stations: each clamp screw's Ø3.3 clearance hole stands on the shared attachment station, 4 mm in from the bare outside face at the shell's Ø8 boss centre. The plain casing face reserves 0.30 mm for foil inside the enclosure envelope, leaving 2.04–2.05 mm of wall below the head pocket floor.
alternatives: Moving the stations inboard moves the shell's bosses and every cap's and lid's holes, Derek's printed shell among them. Moving the outside face outward spends the reserved foil allowance. Carrying the head pocket's outward slot down through the plate removes the wall and leaves the screw's floor open to the side.
