[thin] Deliberate functional C2 spring section: these three ranked surface groups belong to the four free jaws above the tube equators. Their measured 2.400 mm wall is the C2 section Derek selected with the 6.35 mm bore on Mark2 task 1379240291, recorded in future/snap-fit-tests/2026-10-26-mark2-combined/physical-result.json. The ordinary stock below the equators is one broad filled base; the upper jaws retain this specific flexure exception. This answer preserves the thinness ranking and establishes no full-lid force or lifetime result.
alternatives: Increasing the jaws to 3 mm while keeping the same bore increases each outer radius by 0.6 mm and consumes 1.2 mm of the pair's spread space. Preserving the current conservative 1 mm-per-jaw envelope and its 0.35 mm opposing gap then requires wider tube spacing and another routing change, as well as retuning the accepted spring section. Filling above the equators joins the free jaws and closes the press-in mouths. A rigid cradle with a separate closure adds a part and an assembly step instead of providing the selected direct snap.
file: hardware/printed-parts/cold-core/foam-cap/foam-cap-lid-top.step
